From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopfire <hgrmeanwhile@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:22:36 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(acp): surface a bundled Oh My Pi registry entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Oh My Pi (omp) is ACP-native but its entry is still pending in the
official ACP Registry, so it cannot be installed through the generic
ACP Registry flow.

Registry entries can now be bundled with the app: bundledAcpAgents.ts
ships the omp entry (npx @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent@18.2.3, run with
`acp`), and the catalog merge appends bundled entries to the fetched
index after running them through the same schema validation as fetched
entries. Precedence rule: the fetched (or cached) Registry is
authoritative — the first entry with a given id wins, so a bundled
entry only fills gaps and an official listing automatically takes over
once it is published. Validation failures in either source drop the
entry the same way. The on-disk cache keeps storing the raw fetched
text; merging happens in memory only.

Also updates two existing search tests whose exact-result assertions
now legitimately include the bundled entry alongside fetched results.
